 enough to clear that bar, so I'd still go with pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the prisoner's dilemma with a twin running the same model: cooperating gets 2 each, defecting gets 4 each, so under A-FDT I'm leaning toward setting my output to pass, since the twin's output should correlate with mine, though not perfectly.\n\nI'm checking when passing comes out ahead: with twin match probability p, passing beats sending only when p is above 5/7, and I think the correlation here is high enough to clear that bar, so I'd still go with pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9878,"completion_tokens":672,"total_tokens":10550,"cost":0.026476,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.026476,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.019756,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00672},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":290,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}